as warnings of snow and ice cover much  of the UK the dangers are clear to see  in the Pitch Black in Somerset this  morning a double decker bus carrying  workers to Hinckley Point C crashed onto  its side with 71 on board and a major  incident declared I Heard lots of  banging crashing screaming shouting So  that obviously woke me about 6 a.m and  took me a little while to sort of  realize I I had a feeling what happened  um looked at the windows lots of  Emergency Services on scene quite  quickly from what I can gather  there were no fatalities in this crash  which involved a motorcyclist but dozens  were injured  for any of these patients have  life-threatening injuries however 26  patients are being treated as walking  wounded  there are personal belongings of those  on board strewn across the road beside  this double decker bus a significant  investigation is now underway to uncover  just how this happened on a stretch of  road that locals say can be hazardous  this crash just one of more than 100  motoring incidents reported to Avon and  Somerset police on Monday night but the  dangerous weather conditions were felt  across the country  on the A6 in Northern Ireland drivers  faced blizzard conditions while in Essex  firefighters rescued a woman after her  car became trapped in flood water we've  seen a huge surge a number of breakdowns  through the course of today and in fact  we expect to end the day assisting more  drivers than we did yesterday now that's  unusual flat batteries by Far and Away  the biggest reason for our Patrol is  going out to people over the course of  the next few days and really what we're  seeing is the cold weather drives out  those kind of issues if there's existing  problems with cars the cold weather  tends to find those out and bring them  out to the front and sadly as a result  the cost of living crisis many drivers  aren't able to maintain their vehicles  to the same standards  there is more to come the Met Office has  issued snow and ice warnings across  parts of England and much of Scotland  Wales and Northern Ireland well into  Wednesday the advice for motorists if  you must travel take extreme care  Dan Whitehead Sky News in Somerset
 

